{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Pharaoh will not heed you.</b> And if you say: but we find that he did heed, as it is written, 'And Pharaoh rose up at night and said to them: Rise up, go out,' etc. — rather, this was already stated at the beginning of the matter, in the episode of the bush: 'And HaShem said to Moses, Pharaoh will not heed you, in order to multiply My signs.' And in the foreign language (Old French), 'ieougi dit,' as I shall explain." "<b>Pharaoh will not heed you.</b> Another interpretation: 'Pharaoh will not heed you' — he should not have waited for this plague, and he should have understood that it is harsher than all of them, and that he must send you away, for you warned him about it from the start: 'lest He confront us with plague or sword.' And the reason 'Pharaoh will not heed you' now — 'in order to multiply My signs' — is the plague of the firstborn along with the rest of the plagues."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The Old French gloss 'איאוגידי״ט' is transliterated as in the manuscript; the phrase 'אמש״ה' is an abbreviation for 'אני משמעו' = 'as I shall explain/exposit,' though the intended Old French word is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:03.207939361Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}